WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.483
Hey, truckers!

00:00:06.483 --> 00:00:11.083
We're excited to bring you the 1.60 update
for Euro Truck Simulator 2,

00:00:11.083 --> 00:00:14.166
which is now officially released
and available on Steam.

00:00:14.166 --> 00:00:16.250
Game Radio

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:20.600
With update 1.60,
we are introducing Game Radio,

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.950
a brand new in-game radio system

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:27.266
designed to make every drive feel
more immersive and authentic.

00:00:27.266 --> 00:00:31.150
At launch, players can tune in to Pump It,

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.166
Rust FM,

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:35.266
Roadio,

00:00:35.266 --> 00:00:37.533
Pop Gear,

00:00:37.533 --> 00:00:38.916
and Escape.

00:00:38.916 --> 00:00:42.033
Each station features
carefully curated tracks

00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:45.633
hand-picked to hold up
across many hours on the road.

00:00:45.633 --> 00:00:49.616
Escape is also a radio station designed
to help content creators

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:53.916
and we are committed to do our best
to keep it stream-safe.

00:00:53.916 --> 00:00:57.483
Game Radio also introduces
a new in-game widget

00:00:57.483 --> 00:00:59.283
displaying station info,

00:00:59.283 --> 00:01:02.950
track titles, and artist names
while driving.

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:04.716
Players can customize widget behavior

00:01:04.716 --> 00:01:08.150
through the widget option menu
by clicking F6.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:15.200
Improved Material System

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.366
The Improved Material System
significantly improves the lighting

00:01:19.366 --> 00:01:24.266
and visual quality of vehicle interiors
in selected trucks.

00:01:24.266 --> 00:01:28.933
Its main focus is to enhance
how interior materials react to light,

00:01:28.933 --> 00:01:31.183
which will result in a more readable,

00:01:31.183 --> 00:01:34.766
detailed and visually pleasing
cabin environment.

00:01:34.766 --> 00:01:37.383
One of the most significant changes
we implemented

00:01:37.383 --> 00:01:41.833
was a redesign of the materials
used in vehicle interiors.

00:01:41.833 --> 00:01:46.416
As a result, it makes differences
between materials such as leather,

00:01:46.416 --> 00:01:50.533
fabric, plastic, and metal
far more apparent

00:01:50.533 --> 00:01:52.483
even in low light conditions.

00:01:52.483 --> 00:01:56.033
The first trucks to benefit
from the improved material systems

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:59.633
in Euro Truck Simulator 2
are the DAF NGD

00:01:59.633 --> 00:02:02.900
and the MAN TGX 2020 models.

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:04.266
With future updates,

00:02:04.266 --> 00:02:08.866
we will gradually add this technology
for other trucks across both games.

00:02:08.866 --> 00:02:11.266
As part of the improved material system,

00:02:11.266 --> 00:02:14.483
we have also carried out
minor adjustments to the global lighting.

00:02:15.283 --> 00:02:19.216
Volvo FH Series 6 Update

00:02:19.216 --> 00:02:22.500
With this update, truckers
will be able to customize

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:28.733
their Volvo FH series 6 with a selection
of several new aerodynamic parts,

00:02:28.733 --> 00:02:32.316
including the newly designed
aerodynamic roof deflectors

00:02:32.316 --> 00:02:38.616
available for the sleeper cab,
Globetrotter and Globetrotter XL cab variants.

00:02:38.616 --> 00:02:40.433
Alongside these additions,

00:02:40.433 --> 00:02:43.433
all aero cabin variants
will also have the option

00:02:43.433 --> 00:02:47.466
to add the new distinctive black
aerodynamic A-pillar trim,

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:52.133
as featured on the newest
generation of Volvo FH trucks.

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:54.550
Job Details Widget

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:59.083
Based on feedback from our best community
ever and upcoming widget designs,

00:02:59.083 --> 00:03:03.233
the Job Details widget is introduced
with the 1.60 update.

00:03:03.233 --> 00:03:06.366
Its primary purpose is to enable a new,

00:03:06.366 --> 00:03:10.883
more immediate and concise
way of displaying relevant job info.

00:03:10.883 --> 00:03:13.883
Also, in response to community feedback,

00:03:13.883 --> 00:03:18.633
the GPS will now display the estimated
arrival day and time

00:03:18.633 --> 00:03:21.833
along with the remaining travel
time and distance.

00:03:21.833 --> 00:03:24.200
You'll be able to enable
the Job Details Widget

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.566
through the Widget Options menu
by clicking F6.

00:03:27.566 --> 00:03:30.016
The widget will display
key job information

00:03:30.016 --> 00:03:34.150
including cargo type and weight,
delivery location,

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:36.516
job income which is color highlighted,

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:39.233
and the remaining time
to complete the job.

00:03:39.233 --> 00:03:42.083
So players will have this
information available immediately

00:03:42.083 --> 00:03:44.783
without the necessity
to pause the game.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.033
Expanded Rest Mechanic

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:50.100
This new feature gives players

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:53.850
greater control over their rest periods
by allowing them to choose

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:57.566
how long they want to sleep,
and exactly when they want to wake up.

00:03:58.366 --> 00:04:02.100
Alongside this change,
the fatigue system will now be split

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:07.616
into two separate values:
rest state and mandatory break.

00:04:07.616 --> 00:04:10.833
The rest state, symbolized by a bed icon,

00:04:10.833 --> 00:04:15.050
will now gradually deplete
rather than recover over time.

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:18.716
Extended periods of driving
will steadily reduce the rest state,

00:04:18.716 --> 00:04:22.050
while resting will restore it
at a faster rate.

00:04:22.766 --> 00:04:26.500
The mandatory brake system,
indicated by a P icon,

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:29.366
along with the remaining hours
before of acquired stop,

00:04:29.366 --> 00:04:31.333
will function
more strictly.

00:04:31.333 --> 00:04:33.083
In Euro Truck simulator 2

00:04:33.083 --> 00:04:35.166
drivers may drive for up to ten hours

00:04:35.166 --> 00:04:37.200
before taking a mandatory break,

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.500
which requires nine consecutive hours of rest.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:41.900
Sweet dreams.

00:04:43.066 --> 00:04:46.566
We hope that you enjoy everything
that 1.60 delivers.

00:04:46.566 --> 00:04:50.533
To learn more about these changes,
check out the full changelog and details

00:04:50.533 --> 00:04:55.133
at our official blog site
at blog.scssoft.com.

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:57.616
Oh, and don't forget
to give our socials a follow,

00:04:57.616 --> 00:05:01.450
some of which you can find on screen now
and in the description below,

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:02.766
or if you're always on the road,

00:05:02.766 --> 00:05:05.416
subscribe to our newsletter
to stay informed.

00:05:05.416 --> 00:05:09.433
Just head to scssoft.com/newsletter
to subscribe.

00:05:09.433 --> 00:05:10.466
Until next time.

00:05:10.466 --> 00:05:13.050
My name's been Alex,
one of your community managers

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:16.516
here at SCS software,
and I'll see you on the road.

